 {id:"u137a",title:"Celebrations, part 1",items:[["En Año Nuevo comemos doce uvas a medianoche.","At New Year we eat twelve grapes at midnight."],["Cada uva es un deseo para el año que empieza.","Each grape is a wish for the year that’s starting."],["La Guelaguetza se celebra en julio en Oaxaca.","The Guelaguetza is celebrated in July in Oaxaca."],["El doce de diciembre miles de personas visitan la Basílica.","On the twelfth of December thousands of people visit the Basilica."],["En el Grito todos gritamos ¡Viva México!","At the Grito everyone shouts \"Long live Mexico!\""],["Los niños piden su calaverita en noviembre.","Children ask for their calaverita treat in November."],["En las posadas cantamos para pedir posada.","At the posadas we sing to ask for shelter."],["Para la fiesta del pueblo hay feria y jaripeo.","For the village festival there’s a fair and a rodeo."],["El carnaval de Veracruz dura varios días.","The Veracruz carnival lasts several days."],["Brindamos por los novios con tequila.","We toasted the bride and groom with tequila."]]}
