 {id:"u196a",title:"In the garden and the kitchen, part 1",items:[["Sembré cilantro, chile y jitomate en macetas.","I planted coriander, chilli and tomatoes in pots."],["Hago composta con las cáscaras de fruta y verdura.","I make compost from fruit and vegetable peel."],["Hay que podar el limonero antes de la primavera.","The lime tree needs pruning before spring."],["Las plagas se comieron todas las hojas del rosal.","Pests ate all the leaves of the rose bush."],["Riego por goteo para no desperdiciar agua.","I use drip irrigation so as not to waste water."],["Mi abuela hacía mermelada de guayaba y la guardaba en frascos.","My grandmother made guava jam and kept it in jars."],["Congelo las tortillas para que no se echen a perder.","I freeze the tortillas so they don’t go off."],["Los chiles se ponen a secar al sol.","The chillies are left to dry in the sun."],["La hierbabuena se extiende por todo el jardín si no la controlas.","Mint spreads all over the garden if you don’t control it."],["Cosechamos más calabazas de las que podíamos comer.","We harvested more squash than we could eat."]]}
